{{collapse list|Pushing for a law which is unpopular with one or more powerful interest groups is the easiest way to create a strong revolution, particularly if the {{icon|Armed Forces|3=1}} is one of them.|For example, as {{flag|Japan}}, reform the government to include the {{icon|Intelligentsia|3=1}}, and push for {{law|Presidential Republic}}. The {{icon|armed forces}} Shogunate will be upset and likely launch a revolution. When the revolution begins, during the opening moves phase of the diplomatic play you can switch to play as the revolutionary side. The Shogunate is much stronger than Intelligentsia, so you can easily crush them.}}
It is only possible to switch sides in the first phase of the revolution diplomatic play.

- id=\"Risorgimento\"

{{collapse list|''The Paris Commune'' journal entry requires the following to activate:|
** Has researched {{technology|Socialism|text=link}} and {{technology|Anarchism|text=link}}
** Île-de-France has {{red|20%}} {{iconify|turmoil|state status}}
** Either:
*** Has capitulated or white-peaced in the last 5 years
*** A French {{iconify|homeland|state status}} is owned by another country
This means to provoke the Paris Commune rebellion, France has to lose a war on purpose. One way is to join a war with no impact on France, and immediately capitulate as soon as it starts.}}
{{icon|votpb|w=36px}}

- id=\"Emperor Norton\"

Completing the entry requires fully owning all French {{iconify|homelands|state status}}, as well as Wallonia, Flanders, Rhineland, and North Rhine.<br>The first available ideology to start the JE is {{iconify|Bonapartist|ideology}}, which can be achieved by picking them at the [[French content#Divided Monarchists|Divided Monarchy]] JE, and getting Napoleon as king. {{icon|Armed Forces|3=1}} are the likely candidate, which will be strengthened by conquering {{flag|Algeria}}. The rest can be achieved by overpromoting and overhiring generals. The Bonapartists don't have to stay in power, only once must they cross the 20% threshold.
{{icon|votpb|w=36px}}

- id=\"Huge Ego, Sorry\"

{{collapse list|Max Stirner is created as an agitator by the journal entry ''The Nihilist Movement'', if activated between 1844 and 1866 (inclusive)|
* The journal entry activates with the following conditions:
** Has researched {{technology|Realism|text=link}}
** Has {{red|not}} researched {{technology|Socialism|text=link}}
** Has an empty {{iconify|Agitator|role}} slot
** Has enacted {{law|State Religion|text=link}}
** Has enacted either {{law|Monarchy|text=link}} or {{law|Theocracy|text=link}}
** Has enacted either {{law|Autocracy|text=link}} or {{law|Oligarchy|text=link}}
** The {{icon|Intelligentsia|3=1}} is {{red|not}} {{iconify|marginalized|political}} and has approval less than 0
}}The name of the achievement is in reference to that when Max Stirner becomes chancellor and the government adopts State Atheism, Germany becomes \"Union Of Egoists\" and also adopts the Anarcho-Egoist flag
{{icon|votpb|w=36px}}

- id=\"It Never Ends\"

Note that you need to be a {{law|Presidential Republic|text=link}} in order to get this achievement; other republics, such as {{law|Council Republic|text=link}} do not count. It is possible to get the achievement by completing \"Stamp Out Monarchism\" first and then getting {{law|Presidential Republic|text=link}}.
{{icon|votpb|w=36px}}

